# Story 22: Loop Detection (30s)
# Hook: Rysh detects when the AI gets stuck in a loop and breaks it out.
# Duration: 30s
# Source: story-22-loop-detection.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- you land in shell mode.

[00:04.0 --> 00:08.0]
The orchestrator watches for repetitive tool calls.

[00:08.0 --> 00:13.0]
It tracks the last 20 tool calls in a sliding window.

[00:13.0 --> 00:18.0]
After 3 identical calls in a row, execution is blocked.

[00:18.0 --> 00:23.0]
The AI is told to try a different approach.

[00:23.0 --> 00:27.0]
The sliding window means no permanent penalty -- old calls age out naturally.

[00:27.0 --> 00:30.0]
Loop detection keeps the AI productive, not stuck.

